<p>Iran says it has closed the Strait of Hormuz and warns it will attack any vessel that tries to pass, according to comments carried by Iranian state media from Ebrahim Jabari, a senior adviser to the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) commander-in-chief. The strait is the narrow passage linking the Persian Gulf to the Gulf of Oman and the Arabian Sea, and it is widely described as a critical corridor for global energy shipments. The announcement comes as the U.S.-Israeli conflict with Iran widens. Several outlets say U.S. and Israeli strikes hit Iran on February 28. As tanker traffic and shipping plans shift in response to the risk, oil prices have climbed on fears that supply flows through the chokepoint could be disrupted. Even if some ships keep moving, analysts and industry observers say a prolonged disruption would strain energy markets and trade routes: about 20% of the world’s daily oil consumption transits the strait. For many governments and companies, the immediate priority is avoiding a miscalculation at sea—any easing in threats or conflict activity could quickly rebuild shipping confidence and take pressure off prices.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/led5jWJzRmWc-AuU5RRPRAdf67bqJIywmOGOqO2rR3pfLUlXx4p-3Xb2tLUxAz9yKNcp2NXbgZ1_WxKxCQPWiiXf0JlyF-esmak6pSAFb4C88TFcZuTLhe4K3AWOm-w-xw2JiyKCGM8ksmsCfONzXA8YMvQAayviiPGX2ds3vszp39xlAjsyOXBLrYF7JS97DVFirEZkOILPoACoqe_eb3aMGDY26d9jXzySBgJegRioUlnXXXUo6rtfvEQstpacZQRDsPsnIDc_4TlL4g' alt='Boats in the Strait of Hormuz seen from Musandam, Oman, March 2, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Geography: The Globe and Mail graphic puts the strait at about 40 km wide at its narrowest, showing how quickly traffic can be constrained when risks spike.</li><li>Shipping hesitation: With war risks across the Gulf, al-Monitor says many captains are unwilling to chance a transit, tightening global shipping options for oil and gas.</li><li>Marine traffic: The BBC, using vessel-tracking data, shows how the conflict is already reshaping commercial shipping patterns in the Strait of Hormuz.</li><li>Asia exposure: NDTV says Asian economies face higher oil-supply risk as prices rise alongside the reported closure and threats toward transiting ships.</li><li>Escalation signal: MercoPress calls this the Revolutionary Guards’ most explicit warning yet over the Gulf’s main maritime chokepoint.</li></ul><blockquote>The strait (of Hormuz) is closed. If anyone tries to pass, the heroes of the Revolutionary Guards and the regular navy will set those ships ablaze - Ebrahim Jabari</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC) adviser Ebrahim Jabari: In remarks carried by Iranian state media, he said the strait is “closed” and threatened to set ships “ablaze”—language some coverage describes as the most explicit warning yet. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-vows-to-attack-any-ship-trying-to-pass-through-strait-of-hormuz/article70697103.ece'>The Hindu</a>, <a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/02/revolutionary-guard-say-strait-of-hormuz-is-closed'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>Energy market experts: They say a prolonged disruption of Hormuz traffic would push oil prices sharply higher, given the strait’s role in global crude flows. (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/strait-of-hormuz-iran-oil-prices-us/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Maritime-trade explainers: Alongside the strait’s chokepoint role, maps and explainers point to its proximity to military infrastructure and contested geography—such as IRGC naval bases and the nearby U.S. Fifth Fleet headquarters in Bahrain—which can raise the risk that escalation spills into commercial traffic. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/strait-hormuz-key-passageway-essential-global-energy-supply-130685162'>ABC News</a>)</li><li>Regional economic observers: NDTV says Asian importers face particularly high exposure to supply risks and higher prices if Hormuz shipping stays constrained. (<a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-us-iran-war-asia-faces-oil-supply-risks-amid-strait-of-hormuz-closure-rising-prices-middle-east-conflict-11161700#publisher=newsstand'>NDTV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/strait-of-hormuz-closed-as-iran-vows-to-attack-any-ship/'>Strait of Hormuz closed as Iran vows to attack any ship</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/cvgjnv2y90wo'>Watch: How the US-Israel war with Iran is jeopardising shipping</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/strait-of-hormuz-iran-oil-prices-us/'>Prolonged Strait of Hormuz closure would cause oil prices to surge, experts warn</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/strait-hormuz-key-passageway-essential-global-energy-supply-130685162'>What to know about the Strait of Hormuz, a key passageway essential for global energy supply</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/business/oil-rises-as-expanding-us-israeli-conflict-with-iran-elevates-supply-risks/article70698036.ece'>Oil rises as expanding U.S.-Israeli conflict with Iran elevates supply risks</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/2/iran-says-will-attack-any-ship-trying-to-pass-through-strait-of-hormuz'>Iran says will attack any ship trying to pass through Strait of Hormuz</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/02/world/iran-us-israel-attack-trump/a-top-iranian-official-pledges-attacks-on-tankers-looking-to-pass-through-strait-of-hormuz'>A top Iranian official pledges attacks on tankers looking to pass through Strait of Hormuz.</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/israel-us-iran-war-asia-faces-oil-supply-risks-amid-strait-of-hormuz-closure-rising-prices-middle-east-conflict-11161700#publisher=newsstand'>Asia Faces Oil Supply Risks Amid Strait Of Hormuz Closure, Rising Price